    "notes": "PROVISIONAL. The source establishes that this test predicts mortality and reports score distributions for 51-80 year olds, but publishes no age-and-sex normative table for younger adults. The curve here is anchored at 8.4 points for men and 8.6 for women at age 42, declining 7 per cent per decade, which reproduces the source distribution shape at 51-80 to within about half a point. Women are anchored slightly higher on the published sex difference in hip and ankle range of motion. The 10-point ceiling compresses the top of the scale: plenty of fit 40-year-olds score a clean 10, so the 90th percentile and above is not well resolved.",
